{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4QXbmgMW1YEpTZfvXwLT5","type":"tool_result","content":"14:## 1. The transformations that generalised\n20:### 1.1 \"Read B once\" — amortise a weight read across every row that uses it\n50:### 1.2 Thread-per-output is wrong at decode shapes\n63:### 1.3 Stage more per barrier\n74:## 2. Structural wins\n76:### 2.1 Full-step CUDA graph (F44)\n85:### 2.2 The arena (F44, F83)\n100:### 2.3 Adaptive verify width (F49, F59, F63)\n109:### 2.4 Fork/join the kv chain (F57)\n138:### 2.5 Don't recompute a prefix that cannot have changed — cache the main-KV (ladder 1.0, 2026-08-20)\n237:### 2.6 A selection sort is not a top-k — single-CTA radix select (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n348:### 2.7 Change which kernel the bit-exactness claim is *against* — `index_score` as a register-tiled GEMM (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n420:### 2.8 The one adopted win that is not a kernel — actually serve the head you trained (ladder 2.2, 2026-08-20)\n447:### 2.9 `sparse_attn` — stage the gathered row in shared memory, and vectorise the load without losing bit-exactness (ladder 1.7, 2026-08-20)\n522:### 2.10 Join a side stream where the data is needed, not where it was forked (ladder 1.11, 2026-08-20)\n569:### 2.11 One warp, a 2-D tile — `gemm_fp32` at the compressor emit (ladder 1.12, 2026-08-20)\n660:### 2.12 The kernel that read the buffer it was writing — `hadamard`, staged through shared memory (ladder 1.10, 2026-08-21)\n733:## 3. Precision and layout\n766:## 4. What every adopted change has in common\n=== NEG ===\n12:## 1. The most expensive lesson: a fake +28 % that passed every gate\n33:## 2. Retired by measurement\n52:## 3. The negatives that were really instrumentation failures\n71:## 4. Conditionally retired — re-open after the draft-head fine-tune\n88:## 4b. Killed inside the winning iteration — the radix top-k's two dead levers (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n119:## 4c. Adopted, bit-exact, and worth nothing — the `lim <= topk` early-out (ladder 1.3, 2026-08-20)\n154:## 4d. Superseded before it shipped — the tiled `index_score`, and the cost of picking the wrong reference (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n195:## 4e. The lever that was already applied — `jetson_clocks` (ladder 3.1, 2026-08-20)\n242:## 4f. Two hypotheses killed on the way to localising the prefill race (ladder 1.9, 2026-08-20)\n270:## 4g. Retired on a null before it was built on — `hpb` alone, and the reuse hypothesis (ladder 1.7, 2026-08-20)\n301:## 4h. Headroom that was never there — the `cattn:q_proj` \"free 4.4 ms\" (ladder 1.8, 2026-08-20)\n330:## 4i. Packing the KV cache is a CAPACITY lever, not a throughput one — and the kernel it feeds says why (ladder 1b.2, 2026-08-20)\n388:## 4j. Six ablation arms, six divergences — and a boundary prediction that was falsified in its own gate (ladder 1.10, 2026-08-21)\n441:## 5. What the negatives taught","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43c4cefb-fa47-443e-bc25-0eacbab5dfd5","uuid":"234e9b69-4a6b-49bb-a91e-87eb2b988c0c","timestamp":"2026-08-21T06:45:58.194Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"14:## 1. The transformations that generalised\n20:### 1.1 \"Read B once\" — amortise a weight read across every row that uses it\n50:### 1.2 Thread-per-output is wrong at decode shapes\n63:### 1.3 Stage more per barrier\n74:## 2. Structural wins\n76:### 2.1 Full-step CUDA graph (F44)\n85:### 2.2 The arena (F44, F83)\n100:### 2.3 Adaptive verify width (F49, F59, F63)\n109:### 2.4 Fork/join the kv chain (F57)\n138:### 2.5 Don't recompute a prefix that cannot have changed — cache the main-KV (ladder 1.0, 2026-08-20)\n237:### 2.6 A selection sort is not a top-k — single-CTA radix select (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n348:### 2.7 Change which kernel the bit-exactness claim is *against* — `index_score` as a register-tiled GEMM (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n420:### 2.8 The one adopted win that is not a kernel — actually serve the head you trained (ladder 2.2, 2026-08-20)\n447:### 2.9 `sparse_at